---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';

const apiBase = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_BASE ?? 'https://api.mabims.dev';

let first = '2024-01-13';
let last = '2026-12-31';
try {
  const res = await fetch(`${apiBase}/api/v1/meta`);
  if (res.ok) {
    const meta = await res.json();
    first = meta.coverage.first;
    last = meta.coverage.last;
  }
} catch {}
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Data Coverage',
    description: 'How far the MABIMS table reaches, and what happens beyond it.',
  }}
>
  <h2>Authoritative coverage</h2>
  <p>The curated MABIMS lookup table currently covers:</p>
  <pre><code>{first} → {last}</code></pre>
  <p>MABIMS month starts are set by local moon-sighting criteria, and each year (usually released in October) Kemenag issues a calendar for the next year. This coverage does <strong>not</strong> extrapolate astronomically.</p>

  <h2>Beyond the table: forward computation only</h2>
  <p>Requests after the table end are answered by forward computation:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong><code>mabims-computed</code></strong> — the Neo MABIMS criteria evaluated live at Sabang (hilal altitude ≥ 3° and elongation ≥ 6.4° at sunset on day 29). This is the same rule the curated table follows, so it stays on-method into the future. Months decided by a margin under 0.25° carry a borderline warning.</li>
    <li><strong><code>fallback:aladhan-ummalqura</code></strong> — Umm al-Qura via Aladhan as a last resort, fetched lazily per month and cached at the origin.</li>
  </ol>

  <blockquote>
    <p><strong>Warning:</strong> The system <strong>cannot</strong> convert dates before {first}. The backward-walking algorithm is not available.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Hard limits</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Direction</th><th>Limit</th><th>Note</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Backward</td><td>{first}</td><td>No conversion before this date</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Forward</td><td>2053-08-01</td><td>No conversion after this date</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Dates outside these bounds are rejected with a <code>date_out_of_supported_range</code> error.</p>

  <h2>Monitoring</h2>
  <p><a href="/en/endpoints/meta/"><code>GET /meta</code></a> exposes <code>computed_active</code>, <code>computed_months</code>, <code>fallback_active</code> and <code>fallback_months</code>. The <a href="/en/playground/">live status</a> panel on the Playground page reads it in real time.</p>
</StarlightPage>
